Subject: [PATCH 11161/11362] [outer-loop] Update codex and move
 planner/retro/audit to gpt-6-astra

Operator directive named a 'new 6 pro model' for conductor planning, critical
thinking and adversarial review, without the exact name.

The installed codex was 0.144.1 from 2026-07-10 and knew nothing newer than
gpt-5.6-sol, so it was updated to 0.153.4 first. The new binary offers two
candidates and both were probed rather than guessed. gpt-5.6-pro returns HTTP
400: not supported when using Codex with a ChatGPT account. gpt-6-astra works,
answering a repo-reading prompt correctly in 9.8s. The second probe was
conductor-shaped on purpose, because a long-prompt hang is how codex failed
this project in May and a one-word smoke test would not find it.

Drop-in 70- sets the three reasoning tiers only. AGENT_MODEL stays gpt-5.6-sol:
the bulk experiment tier was not named, and it makes the most calls, so moving
it is a cost decision rather than a quality one.

Applied at a clean boundary with no child running and the last task 24 minutes
finished, so nothing in flight was lost. Verified from the new process's own
environ rather than from the unit file. A daemon-reload alone would not have
taken effect: the conductor is long-lived and its self-re-exec keeps the old
environment.

Stated as unverified: no planner, retro or audit phase has yet RUN on the new
model, since those fire at milestone close. Two probes are not a completed
planning cycle.

Rollback for both halves recorded in the drop-in and in status.md.

